      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "the Petitioner above named through his Advocate Sri  KALE VIJAYA RAJU presented this Petition under Article 226 of the  Constitution of India is filed praying that in the circumstances stated in the  affidavit filed therewith, the High Court may be pleased to issue order or  direction more particularly in the nature of writ of mandamus declaring the  action of the respondent No. 4 to 8 in evicting the petitioner house site an  extent of Ac. 0.05 cents in Door No. 1-105/69 in Sy. No. 159/3 situated at  Munugodu Village, Amaravathi Mandal, Palnadu District by proposing to  lay CC road without issuing any prior notice and without following land ' acquisition proceedings is illegal, arbitrary, unjust, contrary to the  provisions of the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land  Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 and violative of  principles of Natural Justice and violation of articles 14, 21 and 300-A of  the Constitution of India and consequently direct the respondents not to lay  the road by disposes or interfere with in the above subject land;\n AND WHEREAS the High Court upon perusing the petition and  affidavit filed herein and upon hearing the arguments of Sri Kale Vijaya  Raju, Advocate for the Petitioner and GP for Panchayat Raj for the  Respondent Nos.1 to 3 and Sri M.Sudheer, Standing Counsel for the  Respondent No.4, directed issue of notice to the Respondent Nos.5 to 8  herein to show cause as to why this WRIT PETITION should not be  admitted.\n y  You viz:\n 1. Mogarala Chinna Rama Rao, S/o. Pedda Rama Rao, R/o. SS  Colony, Munugodu Amaravathi Mandal, Palnadu District-522402  2. Medabalimi Venkateswarlu, S/o. Raja Rao, R/o. SS Colony,\n Munugodu Amaravathi Mandal, Palnadu District- 522402  3.",
